(footprint "Ebyte_E07-400M10S"
	(version 20241229)
	(generator "aqroot-beta-library")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Ebyte E07-400M10S CC1101 410-450MHz 10dBm SPI module. 22 castellated pads, 11 per long edge, 1.27 mm pitch with a 5.57 mm special gap between pins 3-4 and 19-20 where the IPX connector sits. Body 14.0 +/-0.1 x 20.0 +/-0.1 mm, height 3.00 +/-0.1 mm. Pin 1 bottom-right, numbering counter-clockwise. Origin at body centre; pad field asymmetric - 2.00 mm inset from the top edge to pins 11/12 and 1.00 mm from the bottom edge to pins 1/22. SOURCE: Ebyte E07-400M10S user manual chapter 3, which dimensions body, thickness, pitch, the 5.57 mm gap, both end insets and states 'Pad quantity: 22' directly - this part is FULLY dimensioned by the manufacturer, unlike the E22 manual. Module pad detail from the same drawing: top pad 0.50 x 0.80, bottom pad 0.90 x 0.80. The land geometry here is identical to AQROOT_Beta:Ebyte_E22-900M22S because Ebyte's own drawings show the two modules share one mechanical form factor - same 14x20x3 body, same 22 pads, same 2.00/1.27/5.57/1.27/1.00 scheme, same IPX position, same numbering. This E07 drawing therefore independently corroborates the 5.57 mm gap that was recovered for the E22 from LCSC C411293. ANTENNA END is +Y (pins 1-3, 20-22 and the IPX connector). Beta uses the module IPEX/u.FL with Taoglas FXP450.07.0100C; pin 21 ANT stamp hole is NOT routed. RF DO NOT ROUTE until final RF review.")
	(tags "Ebyte E07-400M10S CC1101 module castellated IPEX 433MHz")
